WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:04.190
In this place so unreal

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:07.820
I wait for dawn to come

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:12.950
Farther and farther, like the sky I saw that day

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:19.200
What a joke this hope is

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:22.750
I acted as if I had forgotten

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.250
Farther and farther, like the dream I saw that day

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:34.130
I just want to know the meaning of it

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.300
Within this scattered time

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:41.100
Along with the breath of ours

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:45.060
And of this pain that never goes away

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.610
Even though the roaring of the sea muffles the voices

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.490
Darkness engulfs everything ahead

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:56.530
The light that passes through our fragile hearts

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.950
Won't go away

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:03.750
We only relied on our compass

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:07.920
We believed you

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:14.760
While we stand here

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.890
We're searching for the unseen future

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:29.860
Zipang

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:33.480
Twenty First Century Japan.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:35.490
The SDF Navy's newest AEGIS class vessel, Mirai.

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:38.910
Sets off from Yokosuka Base.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.830
But just as she entered the Pacific Ocean...

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:43.370
Mirai encountered abnormal atmospheric conditions.

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:47.170
She was thrown back to 1942...

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:49.830
...in the Battle of Midway.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:01.140
Then I, Commander Kadomatsu, Vice Captain of the Mirai...

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:06.180
...saved the life of intel-officer, Takumi Kusaka.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.990
Kusaka plans to alter the flow of history.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:23.870
Instead of the future world the Mirai belongs to...

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:27.210
He plans to create an ideal world, called "Zipang."

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:31.330
What role should...

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:35.210
...the Mirai's 241 SDF members be playing...

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:37.590
...in this chaotic era?

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.880
Kusaka, I won't let you alter the outcome of this war.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:23.470
No, I won't let you dictate the flow of history!

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:24.970
I'll definitely stop you!!

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:30.100
The Living and The Dead

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:36.070
We still can't verify the...

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:38.610
...subsequent launch from the main guns.

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:42.820
The Yamato's guns have the capacity...

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:44.990
...to fire every 45 seconds.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:46.580
If the 2nd and 3rd shots are fired...

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:49.580
...consecutively by the main guns...

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:53.250
...with two cannons a piece,

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:57.340
the sea sparrow simply won't be able to keep up.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:00.010
The only option left...

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:03.550
...will be for the Tomahawks to destroy the guns themselves.

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:08.560
I'd prefer to avoid destroying Yamato's bridge.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:13.690
Luckily, we know that their commander...

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:18.150
...isn't a stubborn imperial soldier, but an intelligent person.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:20.780
Due to his experience overseas, he's always been opposed...

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:23.530
...to the Japan-Italy-Germany Alliance.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:26.620
And of launching a war against the Allied Forces.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:28.160
That, in a word.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:31.370
Is the Commander-in-Chief, Admiral Isoroku Yamamoto.

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:33.580
All we know, however...

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:36.330
...is the historical figure that's been recorded in books.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:40.380
Not this living entity who's outside even our radar.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:45.430
We only have a pile of documents.

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:49.760
We have yet to verify his personality.

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.850
After the battle at Midway...

00:04:55.850 --> 00:05:00.190
Are you asking our Imperial Navy...

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:03.860
...to suffer another humiliation?

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:06.320
Lieutenant Kusaka?

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:18.500
A ship 60 years ahead of its time.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:21.550
Even an invincible ship...

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:24.590
...is no match for the flow of time.

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:32.180
Nothing in this world is eternal.

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:36.850
Yet we continue to search for it, don't we, Chief Kuroshima?

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:38.400
We lose and we learn.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.360
And perhaps that's what we should be doing here.

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:42.900
It would seem so.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:45.360
Admiral, I have one concern.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:48.570
Lieutenant Tsuda, right?

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:51.870
Yes. He takes things too seriously.

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:15.890
I thought...

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:19.310
I thought that I was prepared...

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:21.400
...to plunge in the knife.

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:26.240
Go ahead and laugh.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:29.110
I am afraid... of dying.

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:35.750
Instead of thinking of my country, I can only see my family.

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:39.370
I've finally come to realize...

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:43.250
...how pathetic I turned out to be after all.

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:55.260
And what's wrong with being a pathetic man?!

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:56.220
What?

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:00.850
At the very least, you're much braver and more composed...

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:04.520
...than those who throw their lives away so lightly!

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:12.200
How can a man as pathetic as me, serve his country as a soldier?

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:23.670
In our era, human weakness has been recognised.

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:26.170
Now you've found out about it.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:31.510
It's impressive, that you found out so early in your era!

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:40.520
5 minutes have passed.

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:44.480
What's happening? Did the Yamato heed our warning?

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:48.530
- Weapons Officer.
- Yes?

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:51.030
Against someone who's willing to listen...

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:53.530
...words are the best weapons.

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:56.030
Don't you agree?

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:01.540
Incoming message from Mirai!

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:05.420
It's for Admiral Yamamoto, from Umezu?

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:06.750
I will read it out!

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.920
Summary of our next course of action!

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:12.930
First, Lieutenant Satake and Umidori...

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:15.720
...will be returned to this ship.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:17.680
Second, Lieutenant Kusaka...

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:19.970
...will return with Lieutenant Satake to this ship!

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:22.520
A summary? Those sounded like orders to me!

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:27.060
Lastly, adhering to the Yamato's original plan...

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:29.360
...this ship will lend full support to the combined fleet

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:34.160
...in the rescue of the 2500 men from the Guadalcanal Island.

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:36.240
The surrounding waters are dangerous.

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:38.240
At 2200 the day after tomorrow...

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:40.290
2 destroyers will be stationed NE of Guadalcanal...

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:42.710
...for rescue works as the remaining fleet pulls out.

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:46.130
From: Captain of the Mirai, Umezu Saburo.

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:48.090
That's all!

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:55.010
The carpet has been forcefully unrolled for us.

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:57.340
Is this the same Umezu Saburo...

00:08:57.340 --> 00:09:00.890
...that I heard was nicknamed "Noontime Beacon?"

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:05.560
Yes. That's his nickname on the Mirai.

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:09.520
It describes the caution he takes in everything he does.

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:13.690
He is a very cautious man indeed.

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:18.660
Send word to Mirai from Yamamoto!

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:21.290
To: Captain Umezu.

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:23.540
We have no objections to the matter...

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:27.750
...involving Lieutenant Kusaka, Satake, and the Umidori.

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:29.790
We feel, however, that it is too dangerous...

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:32.420
...to perform the transfer in enemy waters.

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:35.800
We propose a location change to Truk.

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:39.350
They're leading us into the middle of the combined fleet.

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:41.600
I knew he wouldn't be easy to deal with.

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:44.310
As pertains to the rescue operation...

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:46.350
...we will proceed as planned.

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:49.060
Two destroyers will be sent out to Cape Esperance...

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:52.570
...to carry out the rescue operations.

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:56.200
I am most grateful for the concern you have shown us.

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:57.570
We will begin withdrawal now.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.950
From: Combined Fleet Commander-in-Chief,

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:01.910
Yamamoto Isoroku.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:13.380
Firstly, I am happy to know that the Yamato...

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:15.420
...has decided not to attack the US Marines.

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:19.430
Our actions managed to move the Combined Fleet.

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:23.720
I don't think, however, that they intend to return...

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:27.890
...the Umidori, Lieutenant Satake or Lieutenant Kusaka.

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:29.520
Weapons Officer.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:32.310
You do know that Admiral Yamamoto likes poker?

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:35.900
Yes, I heard he talks about quitting the Navy...

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:39.200
...to become a pro in Monaco,

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:41.410
And that he's very good.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:44.700
I don't think this is an elaborate bluff.

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:48.370
And he should know that we have a joker in our hands.

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:51.790
Under normal circumstances...

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:54.250
...we would have flashed our wild card.

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:57.090
Contact the XO and his party.

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:59.340
Tell them we're entering phase 2.

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:01.720
- They should pull back.
- Yes.

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:03.100
Send word to the Yamato.

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:07.600
Tell them that we look forward to cooperating with them.

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:11.480
That's all!

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:14.110
So it's cooperation?

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:19.610
I wonder what the future thinks of my fondness for gambling?

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:21.450
Well... uh.

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:26.040
Chief Tactician Kuroshima.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:30.000
Yes. This is the proposed plan for the rescue works.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:34.500
Shall we send the faster ships- Asagumo and Yamagumo?

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:36.550
Very well. I'll leave this to you.

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:40.260
Captain, we'll return to Truk without the two ships.

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:42.220
Understood.

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:47.600
Kusaka, you misread them.

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:48.890
Yes.

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:51.940
Be grateful to the Noontime Beacon,

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:53.480
you're confined till further notice.

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:55.730
Yes, I'm glad.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:59.820
I forgot to tell Captain Umezu something!

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:01.490
- Operator!
- Yes!

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:04.950
Tell him we look forward to his next advice.

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:06.950
I'm afraid-

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:09.750
A strong interference covered the area.

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:14.080
Communications are blocked after their last transmission.

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:17.420
I'm not sure how they're doing it...

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:19.880
...but I'm fairly sure its coming from their ship.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:39.690
Airon, this is Sea Eagle.

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:41.900
How far to the meeting point?

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:43.990
This is Kadomatsu. We've got 500 to go.

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:45.570
We'll be there in 30 minutes.

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:47.950
We'll be waiting for you.

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:23.070
We haven't done this since cadet school!

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:25.320
The helicopter should be just over the next hill.

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:27.320
Keep going!

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:41.880
XO! Hold on! Yanagi's in the valley!

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:45.800
Officer Yanagi! Are you alright?!

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:06.360
No, please, don't!

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:50.320
I'M... NOT... JAPANESE!

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:56.660
Kohei! To the right!

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:10.840
Yanagi! Close your eyes!

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:12.640
I'm gonna use a flash grenade!

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:04.440
Don't move!

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:11.610
It's over.

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:14.530
Put down your weapon.

00:18:57.110 --> 00:19:01.620
And to think that we came here to rescue these guys?!

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:06.620
Regardless of the circumstances, our lives are the top priority.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:09.620
That was what I said.

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:18.800
Yanagi, you alright?

00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:26.520
- Can you stand?
- Yes.

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:28.890
Yanagi? You're bleeding?!

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:33.980
Officer Enomoto, give Yanagi first aid...

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:35.900
...and help him to the helicopter.

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:38.030
- Hurry up!
- Y-yes!

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:42.860
How's your shoulder?

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:45.700
It doesn't hurt at all.

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:47.700
It just feels hot.

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:52.420
Let me have a look.

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:00.880
Kohei!

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:04.340
Did you just whistle?

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:06.850
What?! Did I?

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:10.430
You should do something about that habit...

00:20:10.430 --> 00:20:12.350
...of whistling when you get nervous.

00:20:12.350 --> 00:20:14.400
I-I-I'm sorry.

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:16.940
The bullet went clean through. No broken bones.

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:18.940
Stop the bleeding.

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:51.390
If a situation arises where you have to fight...

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:53.440
...will the SDF go to war?

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:57.900
Mr. Katagiri, have you ever killed a human being?

00:20:57.900 --> 00:21:00.280
What!? No.

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:03.610
We're no different from journalists like yourself.

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:07.820
We've never been in a war, nor do we want to be involved.

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:12.790
The only difference between us, is the uniform that I'm wearing.

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:22.090
We only follow the orders that we're given.

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:35.640
For the sake of one life, we have sacrificed eight.

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:40.900
I will not forget...

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:54.080
I will never forget how I have stolen your future...

00:21:58.790 --> 00:22:01.090
...with my own two hands.

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:17.200
Passing through the distant time

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:22.440
Just peacefully

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:34.220
Without losing your way, you walked towards me

00:22:35.380 --> 00:22:47.130
How many times have I grasped tightly those small hands of yours?

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:53.730
Not being able to do anything

00:22:54.300 --> 00:22:59.810
I kept on praying

00:23:01.210 --> 00:23:11.650
Sorrow or agony isn't enough

00:23:13.490 --> 00:23:27.340
That's why now as if I wanted to make up... I'm looking at you

00:23:40.680 --> 00:23:43.180
We have sacrificed the lives of eight men...

00:23:43.180 --> 00:23:44.350
...to save the life of one.

00:23:44.430 --> 00:23:47.310
Embracing uncertainty might also mean embracing death!

00:23:47.310 --> 00:23:50.270
That island is still a battlefield.

00:23:50.270 --> 00:23:52.770
Preventing history from repeating itself...

00:23:52.770 --> 00:23:56.860
...shouldn't be a burden to be borne alone.

00:23:56.860 --> 00:23:58.450
According to history...

00:23:58.450 --> 00:24:01.990
Almost all of the Navy engineers lost their lives here.

00:23:59.990 --> 00:24:04.950
Next Episode: The Will of Lieutenant Okamura

00:24:01.990 --> 00:24:04.700
History will be rewritten, beginning now!

00:24:04.950 --> 00:24:09.960
This story is purely fiction. The names of the characters and organizations that appear have no connections with actual people and organizations.
